+## [5.0.0] - Unreleased (prepared 2026-11-28)
+
+Major update from the 4.2.1 source lineage. In-app version `5.0.0`, build `50000000`; expected IPA file `LilaShift_5.0.0.ipa`. The exact source, CI and artifact evidence is tracked in [the 5.0.0 record](docs/RELEASE_5_0_0.md). This entry does not assert that a release has been published or a real device has been tested.
+
+### Added — Wave 1 diagnostics and audit (23 features)
+
+- Device diagnostics (W1, DeviceKit-inspired, MIT): live screen metrics (points/pixels/scale), biometrics state, Low Power Mode, brightness and free disk space, plus an iPhone model table (iPhone 6 through iPhone 18 Pro Max, including iPhone Air `iPhone18,4`) with published screen facts. No DeviceKit dependency; readings use public iOS APIs.
+- Structured log (W2): levelled operation log with search, filtering and JSON/text export. It records only this app's own operation events; it contains no network request records.
+- IPA security audit (W3, WQGuard-inspired, MIT): Mach-O parsing (fat binaries, load commands, `svc #0x80` scan), code-signature SuperBlob / Slot 5 XML / Slot 7 DER analysis, IPA package scanning with Zip-Slip and decompression-bomb guards, a threat catalog with a four-level verdict, a CVE radar (all 13 scores re-verified against NVD — upstream scores were not used), and JSON/Markdown/text report export.
+- MobileGestalt key table (W4): 943 Apple Wiki keys with readable names and descriptions, verified key-by-key against worstgestalt (GPL-3.0, not AGPL), plus 122 reviewed Simplified Chinese names. The table is regenerated by LilaShift's own generator; no upstream file was copied.
+- Network probe (W5, ip-tools-inspired, MIT): ping and traceroute over an unprivileged ICMP socket, with min/avg/max/stddev/jitter/loss statistics, plus egress ASN/BGP lookup via RIPEstat. Private addresses are refused before any request; offline state is shown honestly.
+- File browser (W6, Erosion-CN v1.0.8 / WQFiles-inspired, GPL-3.0): multi-select with batch share and pack-as-ZIP, recursive folder import with a keep-both-or-overwrite choice, read-only cross-app browsing with per-app cache statistics, and a splash-ad path table (all paths marked pending verification). No batch delete, no ad-cache locking, no cross-app cleanup.
+- Navigation wiring: the five new pages join the feature catalog (13 → 18 page items, 59 → 64 total) and the home diagnostics sections (11 → 15). The MG key table enhances the existing field editor instead of adding a page.
+- Localization: 281 missing Wave 1 strings added across all 10 supported locales (1934 keys total); the localization suite is green again. Twelve fragment keys that carried a leading/trailing space inside `L(...)` were fixed in code (spaces moved into the concatenation); rendered English output is unchanged.
+- Licenses: Wave 1 third-party notices merged into `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` (§12) with three new bundled MIT texts (DeviceKit, WQGuard, ip-tools); the in-app notices stay byte-identical.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Version 4.2.1 → 5.0.0, build 42000002 → 50000000. The README now carries a version badge checked by the license CI.
+- The 4.2.1 maintenance changes (ZIPFoundation 0.9.21, localization completion, governance/CI) remain part of the baseline.
+
+### Verification and limits
+
+- CI for this version must pass build, Swift tests, SwiftLint and license checks at the same source revision. Previous 4.2.1 passes are not a pass for 5.0.0.
+- Real-device installation, eSIM, Apple Intelligence, restore behavior and performance have not been measured for this version. No risk-free upgrade or measured performance improvement is claimed.
+- Wave 1 items still needing a real device: the `iPhone18,4` model mapping and Display Zoom verdict, biometrics states, unprivileged ICMP inside the iOS 27.x sandbox, the 14 splash-ad paths, and DER Slot 7 regression on a genuinely signed IPA. Wave 2 (AppleLens diagnostics subset, live monitoring charts, Camlo creation subset, AirCard wallet themes, Liquid Glass UI, upstream pairing/notification-sound capture) is not in this version.
+
